IMPORT `sgba-p4-services`
IMPORT `sgba-versions-acts`

-- The later amendments to the Act that its legislative history lists, read on two days: Act 10 of 2005 (section 26), then Act 22 of 2016, Act 25 of 2021, Act 31 of 2022 and S 26/2022.
-- None of them is on the chain of s 2(1), s 20, s 47 and the First Schedule.
-- Same model as `sgba-versions-acts.l4`: a version is read if it was published on or before the reading day and takes effect on or before the day of the conduct; the latest published of those is read; none gives NOTHING.
-- The base of the Act 10 of 2005 table is the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003). The base of the others is the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012), which each of them amends; a conduct day before it answers NOTHING for them, because the 2003 wording of these provisions was not compared.
-- Where a wording is returned as a STRING, the string names the wording in a few words; the words themselves are quoted verbatim above the rule, from the Revised Edition 2012 and from the amending text.
-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED, as in `sgba-versions-acts.l4`: the published day of an amendment made by an Act is the day the notification that appoints its commencement day was first published.
--   Act 10 of 2005: S 76/2005, 16 February 2005 (the Act itself was first published on 16 February 2005 too); Act 22 of 2016: S 461/2016, 29 September 2016; Act 31 of 2022: S 850/2022, 31 October 2022.
--   Act 25 of 2021: S 250/2022, 31 March 2022 (the Act itself was first published on 11 October 2021); Act 38 of 2022: S 29/2023, 31 January 2023; Act 4 of 2008: S 244/2024, 28 March 2024 (S 128/2008 appointed 18 March 2008 and was cancelled by S 129/2008).
--   S 26/2022 is subsidiary legislation and carries its own publication day (12 January 2022, 7 pm) and its own commencement day (13 January 2022, paragraph 1(1)).

§ `Act 10 of 2005, section 32: section 26 (sharing of facilities) repealed and re-enacted`

-- src:TA1999.S76-2005:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 16th February 2005 at 5:00 pm.
@ref S 76/2005, first publication (src:TA1999.S76-2005:3)
`S 76/2005 was first published on` MEANS Date 16 2 2005

-- src:TA1999.S76-2005:23 | 2. The Telecommunications (Amendment) Act 2005 shall, with
-- src:TA1999.S76-2005:24 | the exception of sections 10 and 11, come into operation on
-- src:TA1999.S76-2005:25 | 16th February 2005.
@ref S 76/2005 para 2 (Act 10 of 2005 in operation, except ss 10 and 11) (src:TA1999.S76-2005:23-25)
`Act 10 of 2005 section 32 takes effect on` MEANS Date 16 2 2005

-- src:BA1994.20030731:795 | Sharing of facilities
-- src:BA1994.20030731:796 | 26.—(1) The Authority may direct any broadcasting licensee or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:797 | broadcasting apparatus licensee to co-ordinate and co-operate, in
-- src:BA1994.20030731:798 | such manner and on such terms as the Authority may specify, with
-- src:BA1994.20030731:799 | any other licensee or any other person specified by the Authority
-- src:BA1994.20030731:800 | in the use or sharing of any broadcasting apparatus or related
-- src:BA1994.20030731:801 | equipment or facility owned, operated or used by the broadcasting
-- src:BA1994.20030731:802 | licensee or broadcasting apparatus licensee for the purpose of
-- src:BA1994.20030731:809 | broadcasting, whether or not they have been provided, or are
-- src:BA1994.20030731:810 | intended to be provided, by the licensee or any other licensee or any
-- src:BA1994.20030731:811 | other person specified by the Authority.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:812 | (2) This section shall not apply to any telecommunication system
-- src:BA1994.20030731:813 | licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323).
@ref s 26, Revised Edition 2003 (src:BA1994.20030731:795-813)
`s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): subsection (2) leaves a telecommunication system licensed under s 5 of the Telecommunications Act out; no power to direct co-operation with a telecommunication licensee"
                                , `takes effect on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `published on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS FALSE

-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1199 | Related amendment to Broadcasting Act
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1201 | 32. Section 26 of the Broadcasting Act (Cap. 28) is repealed and the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1202 | following section substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1204 | “Sharing of facilities
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1206 | 26.—(1) The Authority may direct any broadcasting licensee or
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1207 | broadcasting apparatus licensee to co-ordinate and co-operate, in such
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1208 | manner and on such terms as the Authority may specify, with any
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1209 | other licensee or any other person specified by the Authority in the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1210 | use or sharing of any broadcasting apparatus or related equipment or
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1211 | facility (other than a telecommunication system licensed under
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1212 | section 5 of the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)) owned,
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1213 | operated or used by the broadcasting licensee or broadcasting
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1214 | apparatus licensee for the purpose of broadcasting, whether or not
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1215 | they have been provided, or are intended to be provided, by the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1216 | licensee or any other licensee or any other person specified by the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1217 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1219 | (2) The Authority may direct any broadcasting licensee to
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1220 | co-ordinate and co-operate, in such manner and on such terms as the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1221 | Authority may specify, with any telecommunication licensee in the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1222 | use or sharing of any installation, plant or system, or part thereof
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1223 | owned or used by the telecommunication licensee, where the
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1224 | Authority is of the view that such co-ordination and co-operation is
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1225 | necessary for the provision of any broadcasting service.
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1227 | (3) In this section, “telecommunication licensee” and
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1228 | “telecommunication system” have the same meanings as in section 2
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1229 | of the Telecommunications Act.”.
@ref Act 10 of 2005 s 32 (section 26 of the Broadcasting Act repealed and substituted) (src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:1199-1229)
`s 26 as substituted by the Telecommunications (Amendment) Act 2005` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "s 26 as substituted by Act 10 of 2005 s 32, in operation 16 February 2005 by S 76/2005: subsection (1) excludes a telecommunication system licensed under s 5; subsection (2) is a power to direct co-operation with a telecommunication licensee"
                                , `takes effect on` IS `Act 10 of 2005 section 32 takes effect on`
                                , `published on` IS `S 76/2005 was first published on`
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS TRUE

`the s 26 versions` MEANS LIST `s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003`, `s 26 as substituted by the Telecommunications (Amendment) Act 2005`

-- Subsection (1): in both texts the Authority may direct a licensee to share facilities unless the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under s 5 (in the 2003 text by subsection (2), in the substituted text by the words of subsection (1)).
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the person is a broadcasting licensee or a broadcasting apparatus licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the s 26 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to coordinate and cooperate in the use or sharing of the broadcasting apparatus or related equipment or facility` `the person is a broadcasting licensee or a broadcasting apparatus licensee` `the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act 1999`)

-- Subsection (2) of the substituted text is new: before 16 February 2005 there was no power to direct a broadcasting licensee to co-operate with a telecommunication licensee.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the Authority is of the view that coordination and cooperation with the telecommunication licensee is necessary for the provision of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the s 26 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        IF v's `is the text after the amendment`
        THEN JUST (`s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to coordinate and cooperate with the telecommunication licensee` `the Authority is of the view that coordination and cooperation with the telecommunication licensee is necessary for the provision of a broadcasting service`)
        ELSE JUST FALSE

