-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:84 | Amendment of Broadcasting Act
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:85 | 3. Section 8 of the Broadcasting Act (Cap. 28, 2003 Ed.) is amended by
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:86 | inserting, immediately after subsection (4), the following subsections:
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:87 | “(5) The Authority may require any licensee to pay a charge of
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:88 | such amount as the Authority may determine for the late payment of
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:89 | any royalty, fee or charge payable by that licensee to the Authority.
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:90 | (6) Every amount collected before the date of commencement of
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:91 | the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:92 | purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any royalty, fee or
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:93 | charge shall be deemed to be and always to have been validly
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:94 | collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:95 | maintained in any court of law on account of or in respect of any such
-- src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:96 | collection.”.
@ref Act 4 of 2008 s 3 (section 8 of the Broadcasting Act amended by inserting subsections (5) and (6)) (src:BA1994-ACT4-2008:84-96)
`the Act without s 8(5) and (6)` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "the Act without s 8(5) and (6) (the Revised Editions 2003, 2012 and 2020 do not have them)"
                                , `takes effect on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `published on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS FALSE

`the Act with s 8(5) and (6)` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "the Act with s 8(5) and (6) inserted by Act 4 of 2008 s 3, in operation 1 April 2024 by S 244/2024"
                                , `takes effect on` IS `Act 4 of 2008 section 3 takes effect on`
                                , `published on` IS `S 244/2024 was first published on`
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS TRUE

`the Act 4 of 2008 versions` MEANS LIST `the Act without s 8(5) and (6)`, `the Act with s 8(5) and (6)`

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) and (6) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 4 of 2008 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (v's `is the text after the amendment`)

-- Subsection (5): before 1 April 2024 the Authority had no such power to require a charge for late payment.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the Authority has required a charge, of the amount it determined, for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge payable by the licensee to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 4 of 2008 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        IF v's `is the text after the amendment`
        THEN JUST (`s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge` `the Authority has required a charge, of the amount it determined, for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge payable by the licensee to the Authority`)
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Subsection (6) deems valid every amount collected "before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008".
-- That date is 1 April 2024 (S 244/2024): the only earlier appointment, S 128/2008, was cancelled by S 129/2008 (fork F-BA-09).
-- The rule answers only where subsection (6) is part of the Act on the reading; otherwise NOTHING, as does an amount collected on or after 1 April 2024.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the day the amount was collected, or purportedly collected, as a charge for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8(5) and (6) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST present THEN
        IF present AND NOT (`the day the amount was collected, or purportedly collected, as a charge for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge` AT LEAST `Act 4 of 2008 section 3 takes effect on`)
        THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

