-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:46 | Amendment of long title
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:47 | 2. The long title to the Broadcasting Act 1994 is amended by
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:48 | inserting, immediately after the words “broadcasting apparatus,”, the
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:49 | 10 words “to regulate online communication services accessible by
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:50 | Singapore end-users,”.
@ref long title (s 2 of the Act), Act 38 of 2022 (src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:46-50)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the long title says the Act regulates, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 38 of 2022 wording versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN IF v's `is the text after the amendment` THEN JUST "dealing in, the operation of and ownership in broadcasting services and broadcasting apparatus, and online communication services accessible by Singapore end-users" ELSE JUST "dealing in, the operation of and ownership in broadcasting services and broadcasting apparatus"

-- src:BA1994.20211231:1878 | Appeal to Minister
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1879 | 59.—(1) Any licensee aggrieved by —
@ref s 59(1) (s 6(a) of the Act), Revised Edition 2020 (src:BA1994.20211231:1878-1879)
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1229 | Amendment of section 59
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1230 | 6. Section 59 of the Broadcasting Act 1994 is amended —
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1231 | 20 (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “Any licensee”
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1232 | in subsection (1), the words “, any provider of an online
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1233 | communication service or any provider of an internet
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1234 | access service (as the case may be)”; and
@ref s 59(1) (s 6(a) of the Act), Act 38 of 2022 (src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1229-1234)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 59(1) the persons who may appeal to the Minister, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 38 of 2022 wording versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN IF v's `is the text after the amendment` THEN JUST "any licensee, any provider of an online communication service or any provider of an internet access service (as the case may be)" ELSE JUST "any licensee"

-- src:BA1994.20211231:1939 | Service of notice, etc.
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1940 | 64.—(1) Unless otherwise expressly provided in this Act, any
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1941 | notice, order or document required or authorised by this Act to be
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1942 | given or served on any person, and any summons issued by a court in
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1943 | connection with any offence under this Act, may be served on the
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1944 | person concerned —
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1945 | (a) by delivering it to the person or to some adult member or
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1946 | employee of the person’s family at the person’s last known
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1947 | place of residence;
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1948 | (b) by leaving it at the person’s usual or last known place of
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1949 | residence or business in a cover addressed to the person;
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1950 | (c) by affixing it to some conspicuous part of the person’s last
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1951 | known place of residence;
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1952 | (d) by sending it by registered post addressed to the person at
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1953 | the person’s usual or last known place of residence or
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1954 | business; or
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1955 | (e) where the person is a body corporate —
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1956 | (i) by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1957 | of the body corporate at its registered or principal
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1958 | office; or
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1959 | (ii) by sending it by registered post addressed to the body
-- src:BA1994.20211231:1960 | corporate at its registered or principal office.
@ref s 64 (s 7 of the Act), Revised Edition 2020 (src:BA1994.20211231:1939-1960)
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1251 | Repeal and re-enactment of section 64 and new section 64A
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1252 | 7. Section 64 of the Broadcasting Act 1994 is repealed and the
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1253 | following sections substituted therefor: 5
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1255 | “Service of documents
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1256 | 64.—(1) A document that is permitted or required by this Act
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1257 | to be served on a person may be served as described in this
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1258 | section.
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1259 | (2) A document permitted or required by this Act to be served 10
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1260 | on an individual may be served —
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1261 | (a) by giving it to the individual personally;
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1262 | (b) by sending it by prepaid registered post to the address
@ref s 64 (s 7 of the Act), Act 38 of 2022 (src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:1251-1262)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 64 service of documents is, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 38 of 2022 wording versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN IF v's `is the text after the amendment` THEN JUST "service of documents, by the means s 64 as substituted describes, with new s 64A" ELSE JUST "service of notice, etc., by delivery, leaving, affixing, registered post, or on a body corporate's officer or registered office"

