-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:269 | New sections 2A, 2B, 2C and 2D
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:270 | 15 4. Part 1 of the Broadcasting Act 1994 is amended by inserting,
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:271 | immediately after section 2, the following sections:
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:272 | “Meanings of “online communication service” and
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:273 | associated terms
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:274 | 2A.—(1) In this Act, an online communication service means
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:275 | 20 an electronic service that is, or a part of an electronic service
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:276 | having the characteristics that are, specified in the Fourth
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:277 | Schedule.
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:382 | Amendment of Fourth Schedule
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:383 | 2B.—(1) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, revoke or
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:384 | replace, or add to, the Fourth Schedule.
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:385 | (2) Every order made under subsection (1) must be presented 20
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:386 | to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:387 | Gazette.
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:389 | Transitional arrangements for former licensable
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:390 | broadcasting service
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:391 | 2C.—(1) With effect from the date that a licensable 25
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:392 | broadcasting service is specified in the Fourth Schedule as an
-- src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:393 | online communication service (called the conversion date) —
@ref s 4 (new ss 2A to 2D), Act 38 of 2022 (src:BA1994-ACT38-2022:269-393)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 2A to 2D (online communication services, the Fourth Schedule, the transitional arrangements) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the Act 38 of 2022 presence versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (v's `is the text after the amendment`)

